WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:06.350
Varys: The coin of Aerys, Second of His Name,
had landed on madness.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:10.090
But half the coins of the Targaryens had landed
so.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:16.830
Yet only Aerys would be known as the Mad King,
thanks, in no small part, to the Defiance

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.950
of Duskendale.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:24.920
Duskendale was the greatest port on Blackwater
Bay until Aegon built King's Landing.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:31.900
As the capital grew richer and more prosperous,
it sucked ships and gold away from Duskendale.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:38.190
To halt its long decline, the Lord of Duskendale,
Ser Denys Darklyn, petitioned King Aerys for

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:43.559
a royal charter that would allow him to levy
his own port fees and taxes, which would obviously

00:00:43.559 --> 00:00:46.620
be lower than in King's Landing.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.580
The Hand of the King, Tywin Lannister, refused.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.219
But knowing of the tension between the Hand
and its king, Ser Denys invited the king to

00:00:55.219 --> 00:01:01.090
Duskendale to evaluate his petition himself
rather than deferring to his Hand.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:07.200
When Tywin admonished the king to refuse,
as any sensible advisor would, a petulant

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:13.229
and bristling Aerys instead accepted, traveling
to Duskendale with a small retinue and only

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:15.779
one of his Kingsguard.

00:01:15.779 --> 00:01:21.500
As soon as Aerys stepped within the city,
Ser Denys seized him, killing the Kingsguard

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.090
and the few others who dared to defend their
king.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:30.149
Aerys was hauled to the dungeons to have his
beard pulled and have other petty cruelties

00:01:30.149 --> 00:01:33.599
inflicted on his royal person.

00:01:33.599 --> 00:01:38.490
Lord Tywin immediately raised an army and
marched on Duskendale, but Ser Denys threatened

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.090
to kill the king at the first signs of an
assault.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:47.310
If Ser Denys hoped to force Tywin to offer
terms, he didn't know Lord Tywin, who refused

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:51.989
to even parley until Ser Denys released the
king and surrendered.

00:01:51.989 --> 00:01:56.899
The royal army surrounded the city, and the
royal navy blockaded it.

00:01:56.899 --> 00:02:01.719
Ser Denys had clearly not anticipated such
obstinacy.

00:02:01.719 --> 00:02:06.539
Nor that the king's Hand would be in no rush
to save the maddening king, when, as Lord

00:02:06.539 --> 00:02:11.840
Tywin himself pointed out, the realm had a
better option in the king's much more stable

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.260
son, Prince Rhaegar.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:18.000
After six months, Lord Tywin's patience was
at an end.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.890
Or, at least, none could claim he acted recklessly
if he now stormed the city, and Ser Denys

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.819
killed the king.

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:30.239
But the dutiful and honorable Ser Barristan
the Bold volunteered to infiltrate the city

00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:35.390
and rescue his king single-handedly, as befit
his Kingsguard oath.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:43.250
Tywin couldn't refuse such valor publicly
and so begrudged Ser Barristan one night.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:48.370
Then he would storm the city and put every
man, woman, and child to the sword.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:54.980
With only his hands, Ser Barristan climbed
the city walls in the dark of night and snuck

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:00.569
through the city disguised as a beggar, evading
patrols and suspicious townspeople.

00:03:00.569 --> 00:03:06.420
When he reached the walls of the city keep,
the Dun Fort, he scaled those by hand as well,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.379
even dispatching the wall guard before he
could sound an alarm.

00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:16.319
With incredible bravery and luck, Ser Barristan
made his way to the dungeons and freed his

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:17.560
king.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.939
Then Ser Barristan's luck ran out.

00:03:19.939 --> 00:03:22.079
A cry went up through the castle.

00:03:22.079 --> 00:03:24.409
Someone had discovered the king was gone.

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:29.780
With horns and trumpets blaring an alarm,
Ser Barristan cut their way to the stables,

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:35.302
avenging his slain Kingsguard brother but
taking an arrow to his chest.

00:03:35.302 --> 00:03:40.090
Slipping through the castle gate just as it
closed, the wounded Ser Barristan and Aerys

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:44.790
rode through the roused town, racing for the
city walls and, beyond it, the safety of the

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.049
royal army.

00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:52.390
Lord Tywin's archers raced forward to clear
the walls of defenders, and Ser Barristan

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:58.190
the Bold earned immortality by delivering
King Aerys to the waiting, if not welcoming,

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:01.150
arms of his Hand.

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:07.829
Without his hostage, Ser Denys surrendered
and begged mercy from the same king he'd imprisoned.

00:04:07.829 --> 00:04:09.739
Most men would have had none.

00:04:09.739 --> 00:04:11.569
Aerys had less.

00:04:11.569 --> 00:04:18.380
He commanded Ser Denys be executed along with
man, woman, or child who bore his family name

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.900
and anyone who once had.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:26.800
As for Ser Denys's foreign wife, who had urged
his defiance, Aerys commanded that her tongue

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:30.630
and womanly parts be torn out, and she be
burned alive.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:35.340
It was his first time passing such a sentence.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.590
It must have given him a taste for it.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:44.060
For the king rescued from Duskendale was not
the same king who'd entered it.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:49.750
Many men would crack after six months in a
dark cell, being mocked, prodded, and tweaked.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:51.880
Aerys had arrived cracked.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.099
Now he was shattered.

00:04:53.099 --> 00:04:56.550
For years, he would refuse to leave the Red
Keep.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:05:01.919
Encouraged no doubt by his worried advisors,
since he also refused to allow any blades

00:05:01.919 --> 00:05:06.720
near his person, even to shave his beard,
cut his hair, and trim his nails.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:13.650
He began to see enemies in every shadow, who
vanished only when the fires burned.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:21.580
Robert Baratheon: Aerys Targaryen was the
last of his name to sit on the Iron Throne.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:28.160
Known far and wide as "the Mad King," his
was a reign of instability and terror.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.599
The Seven Kingdoms are well-rid of him and
his kind.

00:05:31.599 --> 00:05:37.220
Oh, he may have appeared to be a capable ruler
at first, but that was due in no small part

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:41.080
to his councilors led by the Hand of the King,
Tywin Lannister.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:48.129
There may have been years of peace and prosperity
during Aerys's reign, but it was Tywin who

00:05:48.129 --> 00:05:54.290
was really running the country as Aerys spiraled
further and further into insanity.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:58.550
The dragonspawn were famous for losing their
minds.

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:03.530
It was the price they paid for centuries of
keeping the bloodlines pure.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:11.980
And Aerys more than happily continued the
noble tradition of his forefathers.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:17.470
As the years passed, Aerys's behavior became
increasingly erratic.

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:23.139
He cut himself so often on his Iron Throne,
many referred to him as "King Scab," though

00:06:23.139 --> 00:06:26.240
never to his face.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:31.680
It was rumored he had developed an obsession
with wildfire, and was known to inflict horrific

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:37.630
punishments on those he considered enemies,
including burning them alive.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:43.419
As his paranoia and bloodlust grew, he had
a bitter falling out with Lord Tywin, who

00:06:43.419 --> 00:06:47.580
had served the Crown faithfully for twenty
years.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:54.250
At least Tywin was able to leave the job with
his life and fortunes intact.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:57.800
Subsequent Hands of King Aerys weren't so
fortunate.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:02.520
Then the Targaryens went too far.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:08.930
The Crown Prince, Rhaegar, abducted Lyanna
Stark, daughter of Rickard Stark, the Lord

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:11.240
of Winterfell.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.550
She was my betrothed.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:18.539
She was my beloved — beautiful and spirited
woman.

00:07:18.539 --> 00:07:22.270
And I loved her more than life itself.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:29.220
Rhaegar went south with Lyanna, hiding her
away in Dorne.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:34.180
What harm he inflicted on the poor girl, the
gods only know.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:38.520
Brandon Stark, Lyanna's eldest brother, was
outraged.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:45.090
He rode to King's Landing to confront the
king and demand his sister's safe return.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:48.520
Instead, Aerys had him executed.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:52.379
His father, Rickard Stark, as well.

00:07:52.379 --> 00:07:56.900
There wasn't much left to discuss after that.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:01.080
Aerys feared their loved ones would seek revenge
for what he did.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:05.069
He was right to be afraid.

00:08:05.069 --> 00:08:09.750
Aerys wasted no time in calling for the heads
of Brandon's younger brother, my friend Eddard

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:14.379
Stark, and my head, too, of course.

00:08:14.379 --> 00:08:18.740
I'm sorry he didn't come looking for it himself.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:24.449
Alongside Jon Arryn of the Vale (the man who
fostered Ned and I as children), Baratheons,

00:08:24.449 --> 00:08:28.930
Starks, and Tullys all called their banners.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:34.620
Once our rebellion began, the Mad King's days
were numbered.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:40.890
Maester Luwin: As word of King Aerys's erratic
and troubling behavior spread throughout the

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:47.030
Seven Kingdoms, Lord Rickard Stark continued
to serve his king faithfully as Warden of

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.920
the North.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:55.010
The proud father of four children, his daughter
Lyanna was engaged to Robert Baratheon, the

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:59.440
young lord of Storm's End.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:05.690
Centuries of peace between the North and the
Iron Throne ended the day Rhaegar Targaryen,

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:09.420
Prince of Dragonstone, abducted Lyanna.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:16.630
Enraged, Brandon Stark rode to King's Landing
demanding the release of his sister and the

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:19.760
death of Rhaegar.

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:25.820
Aerys arrested him for treason and called
his father to come to the capital to ransom

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.210
him.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:34.590
When Lord Rickard complied, Aerys, now utterly
mad, arrested him for treason as well.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:38.310
Lord Rickard demanded a trial by combat.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:43.770
Aerys declared fire the champion of House
Targaryen and had Lord Rickard suspended from

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:48.960
the rafters of the throne room while pyromancers
lit a blaze beneath him.

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:54.380
As he burned, Brandon was brought into the
throne room, a leather cord attached to a

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:59.090
strangulation device was wrapped around his
neck.

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:05.500
Aerys told Brandon his father was a dead man,
but there was a chance to save him.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:09.840
A longsword was placed on the floor just out
of Brandon's reach.

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:15.580
And the more he struggled to reach it, the
more the cord tightened around his throat.

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:22.090
Brandon Stark strangled himself, trying to
free his father, who was roasted alive in

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:25.140
his own armor.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:32.920
The entire court stood and watched this atrocity
take place, Ser Jaime Lannister and the Kingsguard

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.140
among them.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:40.950
The Mad King was reported to have laughed
hysterically as these two noble men were tortured

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:45.090
and brutally killed before him.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:50.140
Seeking to rid the world of all his supposed
enemies, Aerys called for the head of Rickard's

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:55.800
youngest son, Eddard Stark, and Lyanna's betrothed,
Robert Baratheon.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:11:01.870
He sent word to Lord Jon Arryn, who had fostered
both young men at the Eyrie, to apprehend

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:02.870
them.

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:08.960
Instead, Lord Arryn joined Houses Stark and
Baratheon in rebellion.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:14.490
Robert vowed to kill Rhaegar Targaryen and
get his beloved Lyanna back.

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:22.630
Tywin Lannister: As Aerys Targaryen's behavior
grew more and more erratic, the task of ruling

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:26.450
the Seven Kingdoms fell to me, Tywin Lannister.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:32.540
I had served Aerys for nearly twenty years
and as a result, the realm had prospered.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:37.650
The royal coffers were full, the land was
at peace.

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:45.310
But Aerys grew increasingly hostile, jealous
of the success many credited to me.

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:48.640
My power and influence unnerved him.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:54.230
The captain of my personal guard, Ser Ilyn
Payne, was once overheard making offhand comments

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:58.540
regarding who was the true ruler of Westeros.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:03.910
When the king was given this information,
he had llyn Payne's tongue ripped out with

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.180
hot pincers.

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:12.210
It was my desire to unite the Houses of Lannister
and Targaryen through marriage.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:17.420
My daughter, Cersei, would marry Aerys's eldest
son, Prince Rhaegar.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:21.170
Such a union made perfect sense for all parties.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:27.660
However, Aerys's senses had begun to leave
him quite sometime earlier.

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:34.050
Instead of uniting the royal family with its
most loyal and powerful ally, Aerys chose

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:40.810
instead to insult my family, indicating that
such a match was beneath Rhaegar.

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:46.220
Instead, he chose Elia Martell of Dorne to
be Rhaegar's wife.

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:54.420
As if to rub salt in my wounds, Aerys appointed
Jaime, my son, to the Kingsguard.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:13:00.640
The Kingsguard may be an honor for lesser
families than ours, but it is a lifetime appointment

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:05.660
that forces him to renounce all family holdings.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:11.910
This creates a difficulty in naming an heir
to Casterly Rock.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.770
But Aerys knew all that.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:19.040
I had grown tired of the king's constant provocation.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:27.080
Thus I resigned my post as Aerys's Hand and
returned to Casterly Rock with my considerable

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:28.660
forces.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:33.880
When Robert Baratheon rebelled against the
throne, Aerys grew fearful that I would join

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:36.630
with Robert's forces and rise against him.

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:43.450
He thought himself clever and kept Jaime very
close as if warning me.

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:48.320
He sunk deeper and deeper into delusion, paranoia,
and violence.

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:54.830
I've heard it said he became obsessed with
wildfire, a substance which, once lit, cannot

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.330
be extinguished.

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:03.240
Convinced he had enemies all around him, he
wouldn't allow blades in his presence, save

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.380
for those of his Kingsguard.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:14.370
Alas, that proved to be his undoing.

